{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfGHpP7rWuiUz2Y9uD8umZ","type":"tool_result","content":"exit 0\n# tests 4453\n# pass  4453\n\n# ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abf77d4b-5fa7-4e6d-92d1-e21b883a8435","uuid":"1e971cbd-a17c-4e26-a70f-df9dc651aa21","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:29:13.530Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"exit 0\n# tests 4453\n# pass  4453\n\n# ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LfGHpP7rWuiUz2Y9uD8umZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8qSMxEPNXSXYQw4AYGC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lxax4tvWwDebthibwFD69Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 06: player close cancels subscriptions and releases only its hold\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js`:\n  - constructor: `this.subscriptions = []`, `this.serverInfoHash = null`.\n  - `keepSubscription(promise)`: records a cancel that sets `cancelled`\n    and calls the unsubscribe once the shim answers (the\n    media-controller pattern), so a close before the shim resolves still\n    withdraws.\n  - `startServer`: ready wait and server-running wait go through\n    `keepSubscription`; both listeners check `state.playing === playing`\n    (captured at arm time) so a delivery racing the close does nothing.\n    `serverInfoHash` is set right before `ipcEngine.startServer`.\n  - `updatePlayer`: deferred audio-metadata wait goes through\n    `keepSubscription` and checks play identity (covers next/previous).\n  - `closePlayer`: cancels all subscriptions after `playerClosed`;\n    sends `stopServer(serverInfoHash)` only if set, then clears it.\n- New `test/unit/playback-controller-subscriptions.js` (emitted as\n  `playback-controller.subscriptions-test.js`; stubs every lib module\n  the graph reaches except dispatcher/errors/torrent-player).\n- `test/unit/engine-ipc-call-sites.js`: \"closing the player stops the\n  server\" now starts a server first -- under the new rule a play that\n  never started one sends no stop. Behaviour change required by the\n  ticket, not a weakening; it still asserts routing by info hash.\n- `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`: keepSubscription / matched-stop\n  conventions.\n\n## Notes\n- All three checklist items are one change in one function set, so they\n  land in one commit.\n- Ran new file with engine-ipc-call-sites and the other controller tests\n  in both orders: green. Full `npm test`: 4453/4453.\n- Stale metadata waits from an earlier file *within the same play*\n  (next before ready) still fire with their own index when ready; they\n  are withdrawn on close. Pre-existing, out of scope.\nEOF\ngit add -A src test && git commit -q -m \"Player close withdraws its engine waits and stops only its own server\n\nClosing the player now cancels every one-shot subscription the play made\n(torrent ready, server running, deferred audio metadata, including\nthose from next/previous), ignores deliveries that race the close, and\nsends wt-stop-server only if this play sent wt-start-server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short && git log --oneline -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":948,"cache_read_input_tokens":85274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":948},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abf77d4b-5fa7-4e6d-92d1-e21b883a8435","uuid":"0f8e4ca0-5595-4b0b-9081-b5cecd814529","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:29:24.770Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8qSMgN25s3m3WdBrUF1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lxax4tvWwDebthibwFD69Q":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-06-player-close-cancels-subscriptions-and-holds && mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 06: player close cancels subscriptions and releases only its hold\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js`:\n  - constructor: `this.subscriptions = []`, `this.serverInfoHash = null`.\n  - `keepSubscription(promise)`: records a cancel that sets `cancelled`\n    and calls the unsubscribe once the shim answers (the\n    media-controller pattern), so a close before the shim resolves still\n    withdraws.\n  - `startServer`: ready wait and server-running wait go through\n    `keepSubscription`; both listeners check `state.playing === playing`\n    (captured at arm time) so a delivery racing the close does nothing.\n    `serverInfoHash` is set right before `ipcEngine.startServer`.\n  - `updatePlayer`: deferred audio-metadata wait goes through\n    `keepSubscription` and checks play identity (covers next/previous).\n  - `closePlayer`: cancels all subscriptions after `playerClosed`;\n    sends `stopServer(serverInfoHash)` only if set, then clears it.\n- New `test/unit/playback-controller-subscriptions.js` (emitted as\n  `playback-controller.subscriptions-test.js`; stubs every lib module\n  the graph reaches except dispatcher/errors/torrent-player).\n- `test/unit/engine-ipc-call-sites.js`: \"closing the player stops the\n  server\" now starts a server first -- under the new rule a play that\n  never started one sends no stop. Behaviour change required by the\n  ticket, not a weakening; it still asserts routing by info hash.\n- `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`: keepSubscription / matched-stop\n  conventions.\n\n## Notes\n- All three checklist items are one change in one function set, so they\n  land in one commit.\n- Ran new file with engine-ipc-call-sites and the other controller tests\n  in both orders: green. Full `npm test`: 4453/4453.\n- Stale metadata waits from an earlier file *within the same play*\n  (next before ready) still fire with their own index when ready; they\n  are withdrawn on close. Pre-existing, out of scope.\nEOF\ngit add -A src test && git commit -q -m \"Player close withdraws its engine waits and stops only its own server\n\nClosing the player now cancels every one-shot subscription the play made\n(torrent ready, server running, deferred audio metadata, including\nthose from next/previous), ignores deliveries that race the close, and\nsends wt-stop-server only if this play sent wt-start-server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short && git log --oneline -1"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Lxax4tvWwDebthibwFD69Q":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-06-player-close-cancels-subscriptions-and-holds"}}}
