{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8qTD5hvnmQSCNDTKXUw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] After the player closes, none of its subscriptions is left, including ones made by a next or previous file change\n[x] A ready or server-running delivery that arrives after close sends no `wt-start-server` and changes no playback state\n[x] Closing a play that never sent start-server sends no stop-server\n\nTicket 06 is done and committed as `c806d59`. The full `npm test` passes (4453 of 4453).\n\n**What changed in `src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js`:**\n- **Subscriptions:** a new `keepSubscription()` stores how to cancel each wait a play makes on the engine: torrent ready, server running, and the audio-metadata wait that holds until the torrent is ready. That covers waits made by next and previous too. It still works if the player closes before the engine has replied with the unsubscribe function: the unsubscribe is called as soon as it arrives. It follows the same pattern as `openExternalPlayer` in the media controller.\n- **Late deliveries:** each listener remembers the `state.playing` object it was set up for. Closing the player replaces that object, so a delivery that arrives after close does nothing. It doesn't request a server or metadata, and it doesn't touch the next play's state.\n- **Releasing the hold:** the controller records `serverInfoHash` when it actually sends `wt-start-server`. `closePlayer` cancels all the waits, and sends `wt-stop-server` only if that was recorded.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **New file:** `test/unit/playback-controller-subscriptions.js` has 10 tests. They cover closing before the engine replies, next and previous, deliveries that arrive after close, and both cases of stop versus no stop. They failed against the old code and pass now. It passes alongside the existing controller tests in both orders.\n- **Changed existing test:** one test in `test/unit/engine-ipc-call-sites.js` closed a play that never started a server and expected a stop-server. The ticket now forbids that stop, so the test starts the server first. It still checks that the stop goes out by info hash.\n\nI also added the two rules to `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`: every subscription a play makes goes through `keepSubscription`, and a caller only sends stop-server for a start it sent. Notes for this attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed.\n\nOne existing behaviour is unchanged: if the user skips to another file before the torrent is ready, the earlier file's metadata wait stays armed until close. When the torrent becomes ready first, that wait still asks for metadata for the earlier file. Closing the player now cancels it either way."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":86222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1083},"output_tokens":670,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abf77d4b-5fa7-4e6d-92d1-e21b883a8435","uuid":"272d08f8-0763-4aad-a600-3333c161a9d4","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:29:35.891Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8qTCoqjs3BotCnh7cXs"}
